  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "The d-electronic configuration of&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msub><mi>CoCl</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;in tetrahedral crystal field is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></msup><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></msubsup></math>. The sum of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>&nbsp;and number of unpaired electrons is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "7",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The oxidation state of Co&nbsp;in complex <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msub><mi>CoCl</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>Electronic configuration of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mi>o</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mn>27</mn><none></none></mmultiscripts><mi>o</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>7</mn></msup></math></p><p>So, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>o</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mo>[</mo><mi>Ar</mi><mo>]</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>7</mn></msup></math></p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/72c1e895-0f5e-44f9-90a0-9e9499549eea-e8d36d19-fe4b-448f-aa1d-019a46db3226-9884748.png\" style=\"width: 190px; height: 47px;\" /></p><p>Since <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cl</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math> is a weak field ligand, so&nbsp;the given complex will have a tetrahedral geometry with&nbsp;following Crystal-field splitting</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/5b287574-c041-4be0-9fa7-7357f5d2e9fd-image.png\" style=\"width: 297px; height: 155px;\" /></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>So, value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo></math>(unpaired electrons)&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></math>.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
